 execution  it's all right to be somewhere on the  scale of hating them to still hoping  that they might turn it around howard  turned out to be a great example of this  and if you re-watch episode 7 closely  you'll notice how they very deliberately  showed you his flaws right beside the  reasons why you still should feel bad  for him anyway it's our nature to pick  sides based on what makes the most sense  from our experience but we understand  that real people are complicated in this  same way and assessing their worth or  what they deserve is never simple  because howard died and before he went  out he laid out a lot of really true  things about them it's difficult to  square what the consequences for this  should be and that's where we come back  around to the teaser would it make sense  for either kim or jimmy to have a happy  ending and then what would that be i  always thought kim would live because  there had been a lot of potential in a  reunion in the gene timeline after  howard's death in the revelations about  how doing things like this is what  drives a lot of their passion it doesn't  feel like having them come back together  in the end would hit the same way if  they can't help themselves and their  relationship would always become this is  there anything happy about it continuing  i guess the better question is  is there a path to redemption because i  do feel like there should be  consequences it doesn't seem like it  would feel like a gilligan verse story  if there weren't i think there's a  higher chance of it having an effect on  kim and what she does next but feel less  solid about that than i used to in the  aftermath i expect jimmy to go into  cockroach mode to ensure survival while  focusing on keeping his wife safe and  then if the past is any indication he'll  compartmentalize push down those  uncomfortable emotions and then likely  cover them up by fully embracing the  salt goodman persona we know what part  of his future is and being saul full  time separated from kim is a type of  consequence that leads to him becoming  gene both of those bits of his future  are devoid of what made him likeable as  jimmy mcgill and so in a way they are  punishment and it's not just  circumstance and things happening to him  he brought a lot of this on himself  kim is more of a mystery and it's really  hard to say where she goes from here i'd  like to hope that there's a path for  redemption but it's pretty difficult to  see from where we are as far as the  happy ending that's referenced in the  teaser if i had to pick something i'd  say it's of jimmy saying goodbye to kim  and the happy ending being they got out  of the lalo situation alive but i still  want to think that it could be from the  gene timeline and that the last six  episodes make whatever he's talking  about makes sense i can't wait to see  what they have planned and i think  that's a good place to leave things i'd  love to hear where you find yourself in  relation to happy endings and this  complicated group of characters we have  a six week break to kick it around and  i've got more related videos planned to  keep the conversation going let me know  what you think in the comments and what  you're thinking about after the  mid-season finale please like this video  if you enjoyed it please subscribe to my  channel if you haven't already and  thanks for watching i'll talk to you  soon

